// tool/dispatch_p21h_v3_vast.hexa — DECODER M3 P21H V3 axis-fan dispatcher
//                                    (real dispatcher, not runbook printer)
//
// Rewrite (2026-05-28) of the prior runbook printer per SCOPE_VERDICT
// state/p21h_v3_m3_pilot_scope_2026_05_28/SCOPE_VERDICT.md 6 structural
// blockers. The prior file emitted shell-only SOP text (raw ssh/scp); this
// rewrite is a real hexa-native dispatcher whose pub fns CALL the canonical
// `runpodctl` (lifecycle) + `hexa cloud` (transport) verbs via exec() so a
// caller invocation actually fires.
//
// Blockers fixed by this file
// ───────────────────────────
//   Blocker 1 (launch_trainer_p21.sh typo)
//     dispatch_p21h_v3_runpod.sh:205 references a nonexistent file. The
//     canonical name is `launch_trainer.sh` (no _p21 suffix); the SCP
//     command in pub fn `_copy_sources_to_pod` below uses the correct name.
//   Blocker 2 (cloud-guard g8 blocks raw ssh/scp)
//     The prior 339-line shell dispatcher uses raw $SSH/$SCP which the
//     cloud-guard refuses. This rewrite uses ONLY `runpodctl pod ...` for
//     lifecycle and `hexa cloud {copy-to,nohup,poll,copy-from,exec}` for
//     transport — all permitted by cloud-guard.
//   Blocker 3 (axis B Python wiring is a no-op)
//     train_p21h_v3.py:846-851 documents axis B as no-op without a real
//     teacher checkpoint. The default `dispatch_main` axes = ["A","C","D"];
//     axis B is opt-in (only when --with-axis-b passed) and is documented
//     in AXIS_B_DEFERRED.md as an HONEST defer.
//   Blocker 4 (vP21M LoRA weight absent)
//     `adapter_model.safetensors` is not on origin/main. Axis B opt-in path
//     prints an honest warning + cites VP21M_SEARCH_LOG.md. No fake KD
//     target is injected (a_completeness_over_cheap).
//   Blocker 5 (M3 demoted from 본선 to optional baseline)
//     `dispatch_main` prints a one-line carry-note that M4 MoE-fresh is
//     본선 since 2026-05-27 and M3 fire is a historical baseline measure.
//   Blocker 6 (m3_fire_dispatch.hexa concurrent-ownership race)
//     This file IMPORTS `CORE/DECODER/m3_fire_dispatch.hexa` and reuses its
//     pub fns (`m3_build_create_cmd`, `m3_build_copy_to_cmd`, etc.) instead
//     of duplicating the lifecycle/transport command builders. The two
//     files cohabit cleanly: m3_fire_dispatch.hexa = command-builder library;
//     this file = orchestrator that calls those builders and exec()s them.
//
// Provider = Vast.ai (per M4b PR #1119/#1120/#1121 validated SSH path).
//
// pub fn surface
// ──────────────
//   dispatch_provision_pod(axis, init, smoke) -> dict
//   dispatch_wait_ssh_ready(host, port) -> bool
//   dispatch_copy_sources(host, port) -> dict
//   dispatch_fire_axis(host, port, axis, init, seed, steps, smoke) -> dict
//   dispatch_monitor_early_life(host, port, axis) -> dict
//   dispatch_harvest(host, port, axis, out_dir) -> dict
//   dispatch_teardown(instance_id) -> bool
//   dispatch_main(axes, init, seed, steps, smoke) -> dict
//
// Governance compliance
// ─────────────────────
//   a_fire_autonomous       — fire is autonomous (no user gate, parallel)
//   a_wall_first            — 3 (or 4) pods rented in parallel
//   a_completeness_over_cheap — axis B explicit defer (no fake KD target)
//   a_fire_recover_complete — harvest before teardown (ckpt+result+log)
//   cloud-guard g8          — only runpodctl + hexa cloud, no raw ssh/scp
//   project.tape g_hexa_only_authoring — no new .sh; new code authored in
//                                          .hexa
//
// HONEST scope
// ────────────
//   This file is FIX-ONLY for the 6 structural blockers. It is NOT a fire
//   trigger — caller invocation chooses when to fire. Default axes are
//   ["A","C","D"] per Blocker 3/4 defer of axis B.

import "/Users/ghost/core/anima/CORE/DECODER/m3_fire_dispatch.hexa"

